+# Controller: reconcile backoff + circuit-breaker hardening — Plan v0.1
+
+**Status:** Ready · **Date:** 2026-06-10 · **Author:** voxist.planner-2 · **Rig:** gascity (voxist-platform)
+
+## Context
+
+On 2026-06-10 the HQ dolt-proxy wedged ("CREATE DATABASE hq → invalid
+connection / 10 s i/o timeout"). The `CachingStore.reconcileLoop` in
+`internal/beads/caching_store_reconcile.go` has no sleep before the
+single-retry in `cmd/gc/bd_env.go:bdCommandRunnerWithManagedRetryErr`,
+and a dead `cacheDegraded → return 0` branch in `nextReconcileDelay`
+that bypasses backoff when the store degrades via a partial-result
+error path before accumulating `maxCacheSyncFailures` failures.
+Together these allow a degraded store to hammer the dead proxy with
+rapid retries and pin a CPU core.
+
+The exponential backoff (`syncFailures > 0`, 2 s base, 10-min cap) was
+added on this branch in the first commit. This plan finishes the three
+remaining hardening items:
+
+1. Remove the dead `cacheDegraded → return 0` branch (replaced by the
+   already-present backoff path).
+2. Add a circuit-breaker log line on the first `live→degraded`
+   transition so operators see an alert.
+3. Add a `bdCommandRetrySleep` (500 ms) before the single retry in
+   `bdCommandRunnerWithManagedRetryErr` so the proxy isn't hammered
+   at line-rate when the first attempt fails.
+
+**Branch:** `gc/vp-2rfp` · **Worktree:** `gascity/worktrees/vp-2rfp`
+
+## Constraints
+
+- Go tests only (`go test ./internal/beads/...` and
+  `go test ./cmd/gc/...`); no integration harness needed.
+- No new exported symbols — all changes are internal.
+- The sleep constant `bdCommandRetrySleep` must be in `bd_env.go`, not
+  a shared package (it guards managed-Dolt commands only).
+- Existing `TestNextReconcileDelay` tests must continue to pass.
+
+## Proposed approach
+
+Three red-green pairs:
+
+**Pair 1 — dead branch removal:**
+Write a test that constructs `state=cacheDegraded, syncFailures=0,
+LastProblemAt.IsZero()=true` and asserts `nextReconcileDelay > 0`.
+Current code returns 0 from the dead branch. Fix: replace
+`if c.state == cacheDegraded { return 0 }` with
+`return cacheReconcileMaxBackoff` (conservative worst-case guard for
+the otherwise-unreachable state).
+
+**Pair 2 — degraded transition log:**
+Write a test that drives `runReconciliation` through
+`maxCacheSyncFailures` consecutive errors, captures the default
+logger, and asserts the log contains `"degraded"`. Current code emits
+no log on the `live→cacheDegraded` transition. Fix: add a
+`log.Printf(...)` in the `c.state = cacheDegraded` block.
+
+**Pair 3 — 500 ms retry sleep:**
+Write a test that patches the internal runner with a fake that records
+call timestamps, returns a retryable transport error on the first
+call, and verifies the second call happens no sooner than 400 ms
+later. Current code has no sleep. Fix: add `const bdCommandRetrySleep
+= 500 * time.Millisecond` and `time.Sleep(bdCommandRetrySleep)` before
+`retryRunner(dir, name, args...)`.
+
+## Micro-tasks
+
+| id | description | acceptance | est_minutes | slings |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| T-001 | Write failing test `TestNextReconcileDelayDegradedNoSpin` in `internal/beads/caching_store_reconcile_internal_test.go` that constructs `state=cacheDegraded, syncFailures=0, LastProblemAt.IsZero()` and asserts `nextReconcileDelay(now) > 0` | Test exists and fails (`got 0, want > 0`) | 3 | — |
+| T-002 | Replace `if c.state == cacheDegraded { return 0 }` in `nextReconcileDelay` with `return cacheReconcileMaxBackoff`; remove unused `cacheReconcileFailureBackoff` constant | T-001 passes; `go test ./internal/beads/...` green | 3 | — |
+| T-003 | Write failing test `TestRunReconciliationLogsDegradedTransition` in `internal/beads/caching_store_reconcile_internal_test.go` that drives a failing-`List` backing store through `maxCacheSyncFailures` calls, captures the default logger via `captureLog(t)`, and asserts `strings.Contains(log, "degraded")` | Test exists and fails (no log line emitted) | 3 | — |
+| T-004 | Add `log.Printf("beads cache: store degraded rig=%s syncFailures=%d: %v", c.idPrefix, c.syncFailures, err)` inside the `c.state = cacheDegraded` block of `runReconciliation` in `caching_store_reconcile.go` | T-003 passes; `go test ./internal/beads/...` green | 3 | — |
+| T-005 | Write failing test `TestBdCommandRunnerWithManagedRetryErrSleepsBeforeRetry` in `cmd/gc/bd_env_test.go` that injects a fake runner recording `time.Now()` per call, returns a retryable error (e.g. `"connection refused"`) on the first call and nil on the second, and asserts the elapsed time between calls is `>= 400ms` | Test exists and fails (elapsed < 1 ms) | 4 | — |
+| T-006 | Add `const bdCommandRetrySleep = 500 * time.Millisecond` to `bd_env.go` and call `time.Sleep(bdCommandRetrySleep)` immediately before `retryRunner(dir, name, args...)` | T-005 passes; `go test ./cmd/gc/...` green | 3 | — |
+
+## GDPR data-flow impact
+
+### Data added / removed / relocated
+
+No data flow changed. These changes affect only the retry timing and
+logging of internal controller-to-store commands. No bead content,
+user data, or PII is touched.
+
+### New cross-border transfers (or "none")
+
+None.
+
+### Audit-log changes (or "none")
+
+None.
+
+## MDR Class I traceability
+
+Not applicable — not a clinical path.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+1. `go test ./internal/beads/...` passes with all new tests green.
+2. `go test ./cmd/gc/...` passes with the new retry-sleep test green.
+3. Manual: after a simulated HQ proxy wedge (`BD_DOLT_HOST` pointed at
+   a closed port), `gc logs` shows a "beads cache: store degraded"
+   line on the first degradation; subsequent retries happen at
+   exponential backoff intervals, not line-rate; and `top` shows < 5 %
+   CPU for the gc controller goroutine.
+
+## Rollback plan
+
+1. **Git-level:** revert the single PR that introduces these changes.
+   All three pairs are in the same PR; reverting the PR fully restores
+   the previous behavior.
+2. **Data-level:** no database migrations; no persistent state
+   changed. Rollback is instantaneous.
+3. **Trigger:** roll back if the 500 ms retry sleep measurably increases
+   the observed p99 latency of rig-sync operations in production (check
+   the Grafana "bd command duration" panel), or if a test flake is
+   introduced by the timing assertion.
+
+## Open questions
+
+- Should `cacheReconcileMaxBackoff` (10 min) be the right fallback for
+  the dead `cacheDegraded` path, or would a shorter sentinel (e.g.
+  1 min) be safer for a degraded store that somehow lost its failure
+  context? The 10-min cap already applies at `syncFailures=20`; using
+  it here is the most conservative choice.
